From: thororen <78185467+thororen1234@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:19:23 -0400
Subject: build: support a macOS 10.13 deployment target in ANGLE

ANGLE only builds for Chromium's minimum macOS version. Fix the code
that fails to build when targeting macOS 10.13.

GPU families can't be queried before macOS 10.15, so report the Metal
renderer as unavailable there and use the OpenGL backend instead.

This patch is needed for macOS 10.13 support and is not suitable for
upstreaming.

diff --git a/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm b/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
index e31d759cac7883f2d2cfb4def2bc705d3f7eff49..ee12f4ac877d71f28ce7071d569280b33de99063 100644
--- a/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
+++ b/src/common/apple_platform_utils.mm
@@ -108,7 +108,12 @@ bool IsMetalRendererAvailable()
             return [device supportsFamily:MTLGPUFamilyMacCatalyst2];
 #elif TARGET_OS_MACCATALYST || TARGET_OS_OSX
             // Devices in family 1, such as MacBookPro11,4, cannot use ANGLE's Metal backend.
-            return [device supportsFamily:MTLGPUFamilyMac2];
+            // GPU families can't be queried before macOS 10.15, so use the OpenGL backend there.
+            if (@available(macOS 10.15, *))
+            {
+                return [device supportsFamily:MTLGPUFamilyMac2];
+            }
+            return false;
 #else
             // Devices starting with A9 onwards are supported. Simulator is supported as per
             // definition that running simulator on Mac Family 1 devices is not supported.
